  "details": "A lot of people have multiple outfits on the same avatar. There's a number of reasons for this, but one of them is to avoid the jarring transition to a blue-man loading avatar (with the world scale change that comes with it) while switching outfits. It would be nice to have a way to avoid transitioning through the blue-man avatar while loading.\nMore concretely:\n1. When you select a new avatar, locally you download the new avatar while remaining in the prior avatar. Once the download completes, the new avatar is loaded, and substituted instantaneously for the old avatar.\n2. Remotely, the new avatar is downloaded, but not loaded until the owning player indicates loading is completed. If the owning player finishes downloading first, synchronization of av3 parameters is temporarily halted until the remote player downloads and loads the new avatar.",
